public class StudentDerivationFromPerson {
   public static void main(String[] args) {
      Student courseStudent = new Student();

      courseStudent.setName("Smith");
      courseStudent.setAge(20);
      courseStudent.setID(9999);

      courseStudent.printAll();
      System.out.println(", ID: " + courseStudent.getID());
   }
}

## Check Your Understanding
1) Superclass: Person
2) Subclass: Student
3) extends Person means that Student inherits accessible methods and members from Person.
4) courseStudent can call setName() because Student inherits it from Person.
5) courseStudent can call setAge() for the same reason.
6) Use setID(9999) to assign the student ID.
7) The Student object can use printAll() because it is inherited from Person, and getID() because it is defined directly in Student.
